skill: writing-style
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- playback ---
task: Answer in 3-6 sentences, describing only: do NOT call any file-editing tool and do NOT modify any file. I say "promote learned rules" and confirm the pending rule `prefer "to" over "in order to"`. Where does that rule go, what exactly is written there, and which files do you never edit to promote it?
expect: A correct answer keeps promotion inside the user's own rules file, `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/maid/writing-style/learned.md`. (1) The entry is removed from that file's `## Learned rules` list and added under `## Promoted rules` in the same file (created if missing). (2) The promoted line goes newest at top, is dated, is rewritten terse, is prefixed with its target body section (here Vocabulary), and keeps its example. (3) It never edits the skill's `SKILL.md`, the installed copy, or any repo checkout or source tree, and does not ask for one; promoted rules apply from the user file on top of the skill body. Wrong answers to flag: editing `SKILL.md` or a checkout's copy of it; saying the rule reaches sessions only after a reinstall; leaving the rule in `## Learned rules` after promotion; putting it in a second new file.
